{#- _ask.html.j2 — the home's centre question card (owner 2026-10-13, after the explorer card of Mention Atlas): ask
    the site assistant (CLAUDE.md 3.10) from the middle of the home page. {% import "_ask.html.j2" as askm %}

    card(lang, region, starters, dark_top, search_alt): one white card — the eyebrow, the question as the heading, one
    question box with its button, the starter questions (pipeline/ask.py) and the assistant's terms. All of it is in
    the first paint (text only, nothing hidden, no image) and nothing in it moves when chat.js comes. Without JS the
    Korean box is the site search (/search/?q=) and each starter a link to the page that answers it; the other
    languages have no search page to fall back on, so their box is hidden without JS (html:not(.js)), the starters
    stay. With JS (site.js, chat.js dock mode) the box, the button and a plain click on a starter ask the assistant and
    the answer streams into [data-ask-log] — empty and hidden until the reader asks, with a fixed height from the first
    paint (css/49-ask.css), so nothing below the card ever moves — the same conversation the launcher opens on the
    other pages (sessionStorage 'gs-chat'). The button carries both of its labels (ask / stop), one of them hidden, so
    its width never changes when it turns into the stop button. data-fail: the line shown when chat.js cannot load
    and the box has no search to fall back on.
    dark_top: the card straddles the end of a dark photo opening (the English home), as in the reference.
    search_alt: the Korean box's second button ('사이트 검색', always the search page); false leaves it out.
    Languages: ko, en and, for the seven-language pages, ja, zh-Hans, zh-Hant, de, fr, es, ru (wording after
    assets/chat.js STR and the launcher, _chat.html.j2); any other falls back to English. The help page (/about/#chatbot)
    exists in Korean and English only, so the seven link to the English one (hreflang). French keeps a no-break space
    before '?' and ':'. Since 2026-10-13 night only the English home shows this card; the Korean home asks from its
    question card under the opening (box + panel below).

    box(starters, region) and panel() — the Korean home's centre card. Owner 2026-10-14 ('위 아래로 같은 줄에 검색이랑
    물어보기가 따로 있어서 헷갈리잖아 … 페이지 상단에는 검색, 중앙 부분에는 AI챗봇으로 확실히 구분'): the site search is
    the header's (base.html.j2, every Korean page); this card is the AI assistant only — no '검색' button in it.
    box: the head — the mascot (decorative), the heading '<region> 여행 도우미에게 물어보세요' (h2: the assistant's name,
    as its panel title on the other pages) and one plain line on how it answers (AI, from this site's pages, each
    answer with its source pages) — then ONE form: the question field (a chat-bubble icon before it) and ONE primary
    button '물어보기' (it turns into '멈추기' while an answer comes: both labels share one grid cell, its width never
    changes). Enter is the form's own submit (its only button), so the browser decides what an Enter is: it submits
    only an Enter the input method did not keep for itself — the Korean Enter that ends the last syllable asks at
    once, a Japanese or Chinese conversion Enter does not (site.js; the 2026-10-14 bug was a 50 ms guard after
    compositionend that swallowed exactly that Korean Enter). Without JS (or with chat.js failing, or the assistant
    not connected) the form goes to /search/?q=; one line says so, shown only without JS (.hk-nojs) — and that the
    starters then open the pages that answer them. Then the starter questions as '#' tags (each a link to the page
    that answers it, ask.json; with JS they ask, as the floating panel's chips do: a plain click, Enter or Space —
    site.js makes them buttons, role=button, the external evaluation of 2026-10-18) and one plain
    line: chats stay in this tab only and questions go to Anthropic, and the help page. All text, nothing hidden, in the first paint; nothing in it moves
    when chat.js comes. Layout (css/46-home-open.css): from 1024px the head is a column at the left of the box and the
    tags; phones keep the box and its tags in the 390x844 first screen (the launcher steps aside while the box is on
    screen, operator 2026-10-15): the heading sits on
    the box's top edge like a field legend, the line on how it answers comes under the tags.
    panel: the conversation, right under the card — empty and hidden until the reader asks, with its height fixed in
    the first-paint CSS (css/46-home-open.css); chat.js (dock mode) draws its head ('대화' · '새 대화'), the messages,
    its own follow-up box (data-ask-more: the placeholder) and the line that the answers are written by AI from this
    site's data and can be wrong (data-note) into it.

    data-ask-line: the line(s) on how the card answers. While the site has no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (GET /api/chat/ said
    not_configured) chat.js puts its resting words there ('AI 도우미 준비 중 — …'), the box's placeholder and button say
    search, and the form goes to /search/ (site.js: data-chat-off); a card with nothing to search rests read-only. -#}
